comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:07:04.041Z",codex,Created after reconciling pmc-wvnz so the completed 100/100/100 contract remains distinct from this new four-dimensional reporting requirement.
  "2026-10-04T11:16:57.811Z",codex-sol,Certification pmc-38z4 on CLI/SDK 2026.10.4 preserves the three-dimensional Node V8 gate. Independent statement coverage remains unmeasured and is not claimed as 100/100/100/100. The new canonical launcher refusal branch is covered by a real invalid NODE_PATH file fixture; no threshold or exclusion changed. Existing owner is preserved; this is an append-only certification observation.
  "2026-10-16T04:04:20.960Z",codex-agent,"Current-main audit at aafea5d (package 2026.10.15): Still open; larger measurement change. `scripts/coverage-gate.ts:35,269` and `package.json:140` enforce lines/branches/functions only. There is no independent statement result. The inaccurate equivalence comment is corrected here; thresholds and measured inventory remain unchanged. See design below. Design: Preserve the current source enumeration, type-only exemption verification, and exact Node/V8 line/branch/function gate. Add a separately instrumented statement-counter run over the same authored TypeScript inventory, with source maps verified against emitted JavaScript. Report covered/total statement counts and require exact 100%, independently of the line result. Negative fixtures must include two executable statements on one line with only one executed, an unimported source, an executable exemption, and a lowered statement threshold. Validate Node 22 and 26 and document tooling compatibility before choosing the instrumentation dependency. This requires new measurement and policy coverage, beyond a 100-line repair; renaming line coverage is insufficient.  No item is closed; verification and closure remain with the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-16T04:22:25.342Z",codex-agent,"Release-gate receipt on code commit 443ab9e: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed 610/610 tests, 49 suites, zero failures/cancelled/skipped/todo. Each used a fresh home with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Both report exact 100% measured lines/branches/functions across 13 source files, 169 documented declarations, and passing production audit, package dry run, changelog/date and canonical attestation checks. Thresholds, source scope, CPU and worker startup/watchdog budgets are unchanged. Independent statements remain unmeasured; the known startup-readiness issue remains open. No item is closed."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:07:04.041Z",codex,Do not implement this by duplicating the line percentage under a statements label. Inspect the primary Node/V8 and any candidate instrumentation APIs before selecting a provider.
  "2026-08-20T21:19:04.644Z",codex,"Measured evidence on 2026-08-20: npm run release:check passed 387 tests before the PR #148 review follow-up,and the Node/V8 table reported all nine measured sources plus aggregate at exactly 100.00 percent lines,branches,and functions. The same output contains no statements column,which is the gap this item owns."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:07:04.041Z",codex,Exact coverage claims must name the dimensions the authoritative tool actually measures; semantic equivalence needs evidence when a required metric is absent.
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
